<h2 class="mt-6 l-ui-heading--section">Features</h2>
<div class="l-ui-grid mt-4">
  <div class="l-ui-card l-ui-card--gradient l-ui-tint-1">
    <h3 class="l-ui-card__title">
      <span class="l-ui-card__icon" style="--l-ui-icon-src: url('<%= asset_path "layered_ui/icon_code_bracket.svg" %>')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>Skip the boilerplate</span>
    </h3>
    <p class="l-ui-card__body">Declare your resource and route - get index, show, create, update, delete, search, sort, and pagination for free.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="l-ui-card l-ui-card--gradient l-ui-tint-2">
    <h3 class="l-ui-card__title">
      <span class="l-ui-card__icon" style="--l-ui-icon-src: url('<%= asset_path "icon_paint.svg" %>')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>Looks right out of the box</span>
    </h3>
    <p class="l-ui-card__body">Tables, forms, and pagination come pre-styled via <a href="https://github.com/layered-ai-public/layered-ui-rails">layered-ui-rails</a> with WCAG 2.2 AA compliance and dark mode included - customize as you need.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="l-ui-card l-ui-card--gradient l-ui-tint-3">
    <h3 class="l-ui-card__title">
      <span class="l-ui-card__icon" style="--l-ui-icon-src: url('<%= asset_path "icon_wrench.svg" %>')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>Override only what you need</span>
    </h3>
    <p class="l-ui-card__body">Swap a single view partial, or subclass the controller to customize one action - the rest keeps working.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="l-ui-card l-ui-card--gradient l-ui-tint-4">
    <h3 class="l-ui-card__title">
      <span class="l-ui-card__icon" style="--l-ui-icon-src: url('<%= asset_path "icon_eject.svg" %>')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>Eject if you outgrow it</span>
    </h3>
    <p class="l-ui-card__body">Generate the full view templates into your app to rewrite the markup wholesale - and keep reusing the layered-ui components you still want.</p>
  </div>
</div>
